id: pm-github-lfcf
title: Closeout changelog generation attributes new deliveries to an old package release
description: "Verified unresolved review at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/32#discussion_r4301991646: October delivery is rendered under package version 2026.9.2 and its September heading. Auto-merge must leave conversation resolution intact. Investigate caller changelog/release policy separately from check dispatch and PR freshness; coordinate with import-fidelity PR 142 without changing that branch."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: changelog-unreleased
created_at: "2026-10-17T09:45:00.893Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T16:35:05.001Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Regenerated closeout output keeps historical release sections intact and presents post-release deliveries under the correct unreleased or released heading; regression fails when the release placement rule is reverted.
comments[29]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T06:59:53.668Z",codex-agent,"Read all 15 unresolved threads across the eight reported PRs. Plan: replay current main sync and closeout in disposable repo copies, classify import fidelity versus remaining placement or changelog defects, add a real git/tracker regression and behavioral revert proof, run unchanged npm and Bun release gates, and document Dependabot pin behavior. Related import fidelity: pm-github-c093 / PR #142 / v2026.10.19."
  "2026-10-20T07:07:24.851Z",codex-agent,"Disposable-copy replay on main c651421 confirms imported GitHub dates and historical placement are corrected for pm-brief, pm-beads, pm-context and pm-csv. Remaining defects: untagged pm-ado version fabricates a pending September release during automation, and native GitHub issue declarations in pm-linear/pm-rlm descriptions are not recognized as ownership. Automation now passes --no-pending-release to changelog:full; explicit leading GitHub issue declarations become link-only matches retaining native delivery evidence. Incidental prose links remain non-owning. Historical incident titles still render in Fixed in pm-changelog; document a minimal repro without changing that package."
  "2026-10-20T07:12:37.217Z",codex-agent,"Inventory correction: the eight GraphQL connections contain 14 unresolved thread nodes, not the initially reported 15 (1+2+2+1+3+2+2+1). Every node and each distinct subfinding is classified in docs/changelog-release-placement.md. Disposable main replays and regenerated timestamps/releases are recorded there; related wording follow-up is pm-github-n0mm. Offline Linear export confirms two affected create payloads before owner matching versus one afterward; no provider mutation was made."
  "2026-10-20T07:17:29.894Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in separate source snapshots: reverting only the workflow post-script placement policy makes both untagged-package regressions fail (2 tests, 0 pass, 2 assertion failures; October delivery missing from Unreleased). Reverting only matchImportedIssue makes both plain/atomic native-owner regressions fail (2 tests, 0 pass, 2 assertion failures; identity new instead of github-declaration). Fixed counterparts pass 4/4 placement and 2/2 owner tests. No worktree source was mutated for the proof. Restarting the exploratory full npm gate with the required clean HOME and Git configuration; stopped runs are not gate evidence."
  "2026-10-20T07:19:48.690Z",codex-agent,Pinned pm test metadata updates reject timeout_seconds because the project peer floor cannot safely refuse guarded item format 2. Preserved pins/history and used the supported run-level --timeout 2400 instead. The default-timeout attempt is not passing evidence. Adjusted the existing npm project-directory fixture to terminate Node options before receiving forwarded generator arguments.
  "2026-10-20T07:22:41.456Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification passed: pm test pm-github-lfcf --run --timeout 2400 --progress executed both registered commands successfully (4 placement regressions and 2 native-owner regressions); no skips, timeouts or assertion failures. Automatic test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the receipt without changing that policy. All 14 thread classifications, date/release evidence and Dependabot pin guidance are documented."
  "2026-10-20T07:25:53.478Z",codex-agent,"Strict health comparison: unchanged main and the package worktree both fail only extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew:2026.10.15:2026.10.19:pm-github; both report the same seven stale in-progress items. Integrity and history_drift checks are OK. No dependency or tracker-history repair is authorized or performed; release gates are separate evidence."
  "2026-10-20T08:14:42.666Z",codex-agent,"Full clean-HOME npm release:check PASS: 964/964 tests, 0 failures/cancellations/skips; 16 authored modules at exact 11040/11040 lines, 11040/11040 statements, 300/300 functions and 3520/3520 branches. Docstrings: 176 declarations in 15 files; duplication: zero duplicated lines across the 16-module source inventory; production audit: 0 vulnerabilities; pack dry-run, changelog check and release-publish attestation all pass. Source hashes are unchanged. Bun release:check is now running on the same source."
  "2026-10-20T09:19:53.883Z",codex-agent,"Final npm and Bun release:check both PASS on unchanged source hashes: each 964/964 tests with 0 failures/cancellations/skips, exact 11040/11040 lines and statements, 300/300 functions, 3520/3520 branches across all 16 authored modules. Both pass docstrings, zero-duplication gate, production audit with 0 vulnerabilities, package dry-run, changelog check and publish attestation at unchanged thresholds. Refreshed all eight PRs: the same 14 unresolved threads/comments, no new findings or further pages. Classification, exact lifecycle/release evidence, revert proofs, pin guidance and the pm-changelog follow-up are in docs/changelog-release-placement.md. Existing strict-health SDK skew remains separate; no dependency pins or original history entries were changed. Preparing the review PR; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-20T09:59:10.660Z",codex-agent,"PR 158 round 1: merged origin/main before edits. Fix CodeQL alerts 8 and 7 with exact ownership-declaration parity and backwards punctuation trimming; review all imported-text regex consumers, add 200000-character timing regressions and independent behavioural revert proofs, then run both unchanged release gates. Also found overlapping optional-quote whitespace in the privacy phone rule and an end-anchored API-base slash trim. Baseline tracker history integrity is clean; health reports pinned-versus-global extension host skew and advisory stale items."
  "2026-10-20T10:01:50.910Z",codex-agent,"Focused compatibility and timing suite passes 6/6. Alert 8 uses disjoint colon/no-colon branches and retains mandatory whitespace after a colon, avoiding the suggested pattern widening acceptance. Declaration table covers 13 explicit rows plus 578 separator combinations across JavaScript whitespace; trim table covers 14 rows including empty/all-punctuation/internal punctuation and non-punctuation sentinels. Initial timings for 200000 triggers: ownership spaces 1.318 ms; body parentheses plus sentinel 0.635 ms; privacy phone spaces 35.965 ms; API-base slashes plus sentinel 1.120 ms. Self-review inventory: import-fidelity.ts, index.ts, gate.ts, closeout.ts, projects.ts and refresh.ts; anchored/disjoint or bounded patterns and sticky dependency scanning have no additional same-class issue. Next: independently restore each old implementation and confirm the matching timing regression fails."
  "2026-10-20T10:05:31.645Z",codex-agent,"Independent alert 8 behavioural revert proof: restored only the old ownership regex inside matchImportedIssue and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"ownership whitespace trigger\" test/import-regex.test.ts. Result 0/1 pass, assertion failure: 76924.809 ms exceeds unchanged 50 ms limit for 200000 spaces. Fixed implementation measured 1.318 ms and was restored before the next mutation. Imports use TypeScript source directly, so no dist rebuild is needed."
  "2026-10-20T10:06:37.118Z",codex-agent,"Independent alert 7 behavioural revert proof: restored only the old punctuation replacement in locators and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"locator punctuation trigger\" test/import-regex.test.ts. Result 0/1 pass, assertion failure: 151014.406 ms exceeds unchanged 50 ms limit for an issue body URL followed by 200000 parentheses and a final x sentinel. Fixed implementation measured 0.635 ms. The fixed source was restored immediately. Both CodeQL timing regressions therefore reject their original vulnerable implementations independently."
  "2026-10-20T10:07:07.948Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility proof: with no colon the old adjacent whitespace groups accept exactly one-or-more whitespace; with a colon they accept optional whitespace before and mandatory whitespace after. The replacement encodes those cases separately, with the same URL capture; removed trailing whitespace was not used by any caller. Declaration parity old/new: single space yes/yes, multiple spaces yes/yes, tab yes/yes, colon-space yes/yes, whitespace-colon-tab yes/yes, colon-without-space no/no, no URL no/no. Trim parity old/new: empty to empty; plain unchanged; each trailing punctuation character and mixed runs removed; all-punctuation to empty; internal punctuation preserved; punctuation followed by space/newline/x preserved; URL slash retained until the existing separate slash normalization. Tests execute the production matcher, complete locators path and trim helper."
  "2026-10-20T10:11:13.483Z",codex-agent,"The optional 200000-character privacy mutation trial was stopped after several minutes under shared-host load and is not counted as a passing revert proof. The two additional (non-CodeQL) timing regressions use 20000 characters, retaining the same 50 ms assertion while limiting decoding overhead in the full privacy scanner. Both requested CodeQL regressions remain at 200000 characters with their unchanged 50 ms assertions and completed independent revert proofs. No release-gate threshold or source scope changed."
  "2026-10-20T10:12:06.363Z",codex-agent,"Additional final-test revert proofs: restoring only the old privacy phone regex fails node --test --test-name-pattern=\"privacy phone whitespace\" test/import-regex.test.ts (0/1, 2799.794 ms for 20000 spaces versus 50 ms); restoring only the old githubApiBase slash regex fails node --test --test-name-pattern=\"API-base slash trim\" test/import-regex.test.ts (0/1, 1592.372 ms for 20000 slashes plus sentinel). Restored all fixed source. Final focused suite passes 6/6 after rebuild and test typecheck: ownership 3.141 ms and locator 5.329 ms for 200000 characters; privacy 9.698 ms and API base 0.085 ms for 20000. Separate candidate review confirms unchanged captures, punctuation sets, URL normalization order, match offsets and privacy findings. No additional surviving same-class path found."
  "2026-10-20T10:25:29.080Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification completed: pm test pm-github-lfcf --run --timeout 2400 --progress passes 3/3 registered commands (4 changelog-placement tests, 2 native-owner tests, 6 regex tests), zero skips/failures/timeouts. Test-result tracking remains disabled by existing policy; this append-only comment records the receipt. Changelog generation and check pass. Clean-HOME/Git-isolated npm release:check has passed typecheck, build, docstrings (176 declarations), lint, unchanged zero-duplication gate and privacy audit of 5922 Git objects; full coverage is still running. Expanded self-review includes scripts and embedded workflow code, with no further same-class imported-text regex found."
  "2026-10-20T10:48:29.109Z",codex-agent,"Additional self-review finding confirmed: the legacy OpenAI key rule retries a missing embedded marker at every sk- prefix, taking 3423.552 ms for 6000 prefixes (18000 characters) through scanLineForRuleHits. Stopped the owned npm release run before changing source; that run is incomplete, not passing evidence. Replaced it with a single greedy candidate scan plus a fixed-window marker confirmation, preserving the old 20-character padding on each side and exact matched text/offsets. Added boundary, multiple-candidate and repeated-prefix parity cases. Both full release gates will run again on the final source; no threshold or inventory changes."
  "2026-10-20T10:53:40.979Z",codex-agent,"A separate algorithmic follow-up is tracked as pm-github-4cuz: parseDependencyReferences rescans failed sticky-reference spans at each repeated phrase; 6000 copies of blocks. took 1906.303 ms with no references. It has no adjacent overlapping quantifier or end-anchored trim to replace, so remains a separate parser change. The current regex patch additionally fixes repeated sk- candidate retries in the privacy scanner. Key-marker parity covers 57 cases; its supplemental timing guard uses the best of three 3000-prefix trials to exclude isolated scheduler pauses. The two required CodeQL guards remain single 200000-character trials at 50 ms."
  "2026-10-20T10:54:53.669Z",codex-agent,"Final key-rule behavioural revert proof: restore only the old candidate regex (keeping the other fixes and marker confirmation) and run node --test --test-name-pattern=\"privacy key marker\" test/import-regex.test.ts. Result 0/1 pass; best of three 3000-prefix trials 272.019 ms exceeds 50 ms. Fixed source restored. Lint/build/test typecheck pass; final focused suite passes 7/7: 200000-space ownership 1.321 ms, 200000-parenthesis body 0.648 ms, 20000-space phone 10.756 ms, 20000-slash API base 0.038 ms, 3000-prefix key marker 4.082 ms (best of three). All five fixes have independent failing behavioural reverts. Preparing isolated identical verification trees for the two full unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-20T12:09:15.095Z",codex-agent,"Full validation attempt: clean-HOME npm release:check passed all 971 tests, zero skips/failures, exact 100/100/100/100 across 16 modules (11055 lines/statements, 302 functions, 3526 branches), and every remaining release check. The parallel Bun entry point passed 970/971 and all source coverage, but the supplemental 20000-space phone timing sample measured 58.157 ms against 50 ms; that full run is failed evidence. Both required single-trial 200000-character guards passed in both runs: ownership 11.399/16.987 ms, locator 0.686/0.655 ms. Production source remains unchanged. The supplemental phone guard now uses three trials, like the key guard, while keeping 50 ms and its old-regex failure proof; rerunning focused instrumented tests and the full gates."
  "2026-10-20T12:10:01.948Z",codex-agent,"Updated supplemental phone revert proof on the final three-trial test: restoring only the old overlapping phone regex fails node --test --test-name-pattern=\"privacy phone whitespace\" test/import-regex.test.ts (0/1, best of three 853.318 ms versus 50 ms). Restored fixed source. Focused suite with native V8 coverage enabled passes 7/7: ownership 1.450 ms, locator 0.659 ms, phone 4.014 ms (best of three), API base 0.074 ms, key marker 3.052 ms (best of three). Neither required CodeQL test nor any release threshold changed."
  "2026-10-20T13:58:54.291Z",codex-agent,"Final verification PASS: clean-HOME/Git-isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0 with 971/971 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Each run measures exact 100/100/100/100 over all 16 authored modules: 11055/11055 lines and statements, 302/302 functions, 3526/3526 branches. Unchanged duplication threshold: zero duplicated lines; docstrings: 176 declarations; production audit: zero vulnerabilities; package dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation gates pass. Verified 443 source/test/config/tracker snapshot files byte-identical across runs and unchanged after validation. Required single-trial 200000-character timings npm/Bun: ownership 17.474/7.721 ms; locator parentheses plus sentinel 0.632/3.928 ms. Supplemental timings: phone 18.456/32.200 ms (20000 spaces, best of three), API base 0.079/0.073 ms (20000 slashes plus sentinel), key 14.299/6.433 ms (3000 prefixes, best of three). Final linked PM run passes 3/3 commands, 13 tests; automatic result recording remains disabled by existing policy. All five independent old-regex reverts fail their 50 ms assertions; proofs and parity evidence are in earlier append-only comments. Tracker validation passes with advisory findings, all 143 items have clean history/storage integrity; strict health retains the existing host-version skew. Open separate parser follow-up: pm-github-4cuz. Releasing claim without closing the item for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-20T15:11:17.200Z",codex-agent,"PR 158 review round: merged origin/main first. Retrieved every unresolved thread and all comments (two threads, neither connection paginated); the latest CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range findings. Both findings are valid: release evidence documentation retains earlier totals, and sync placement tests discard the import result. The sync fixture now has an unrelated native title, so only the imported item can satisfy the changelog assertion, and asserts imported=1. The documentation explicitly anchors the final 971-test regex-hardening snapshot to f2dcdbe6eade612288cd783208e5904270e44ab7. Inspect the whole PR diff for equivalent false positives and stale counts, then record independent revert/mutation proofs and both unchanged release gates."
  "2026-10-20T15:13:56.564Z",codex-agent,"Self-review covered the entire 21-file PR diff, including workflow forwarding, ownership matching, imported-text regex consumers, watchdog readiness, fixtures, documentation, and append-only PM records. No additional runtime defect in the same classes was found. Historical focused-suite and health statements are now explicitly scoped to the original placement snapshot to avoid presenting older evidence as current. The native owner regressions remain real tracker tests; this review round changes only assertions and documentation, with no new git dependency or runtime feature. dist is ignored and has zero tracked files; the build was regenerated locally. The original empty-import mutation also fails its changelog assertion (0/2), so the reviewers broader claim that the precreated title alone masks a completely missing import is not reproduced. The narrower missing-result-assertion finding is addressed and is being checked with an incorrect reported count after a real write."
  "2026-10-20T15:14:16.746Z",codex-agent,"Review revert proofs: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"placement report\" test/changelog-placement.test.ts fails 0/1 when only the documented totals are restored to 964 tests and the old coverage counts, with the snapshot label retained. Restoring the complete old report also fails 0/1. For node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^sync:\" test/changelog-placement.test.ts, the real importer still writes its fixture but a test-local mutation changes only its reported imported count to zero: both cases fail (0/2, 0 !== 1). Reverting only the new result assertions under that same mutation passes 2/2, proving the assertions detect the previously unchecked result. An empty fetched issue list fails 0/2 at the new count assertion; even removing that assertion still fails 0/2 at the changelog title because the unrelated native title cannot satisfy it. All mutations were restored. Fixed focused suite passes 5/5, zero skips/cancellations. Tests import source directly; the documentation regression reads the actual report. No SDK mock or tracked temporary file was used."
  "2026-10-20T15:16:30.499Z",codex-agent,"Linked PM verification PASS: env HOME=<clean-directory> GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-github-lfcf --run --timeout 2400 --progress executes 3/3 registered commands, 14/14 tests (placement/report 5, native owners 2, regex parity/timing 7), with zero skips, timeouts or failures. Existing policy disables automatic result recording, so this append-only comment is the receipt. Regenerated changelog after tracker writes and changelog:check passed. The npm release gate has passed typecheck, build, 176-declaration docstring check, lint, unchanged zero-duplication gate, and privacy audit; full coverage is running."
  "2026-10-20T15:21:57.008Z",codex-agent,"Owner-rule non-git acceptance PASS in two disposable plain-directory trackers (git rev-parse confirms no repository): ordinary and atomic imports each report imported=0, updated=1, retain exactly one item, preserve its native title/description/status/created_at, and add GitHub link-only metadata. Real pinned CLI initialization and real SDK operations; no mocks. This was an additional manual acceptance check, not included in the release-gate counts. Current pm validate --json passes with seven advisory warnings; strict health fails only the pre-existing extension host-version skew. All 143 tracker items have clean history/storage integrity, with no drift or pending merge receipts."
  "2026-10-20T16:35:05.000Z",codex-agent,"Review thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6uYoiz corrects and labels the measured regex-hardening release evidence and adds its failing-on-revert report regression. PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6uYoi6 asserts the real atomic imported count and separates the native fixture title; independent wrong-count and missing-import mutations are recorded above. npm and Bun full release gates are still running under severe shared-host load, with no failures reported so far. Bun uses an independent validation clone with copied installed dependencies, no second npm ci, and all 443 tracked files verified byte-identical before validation. Commit and push the focused-tested changes to start CI while local gates continue; final gate receipts will follow before handoff. No thread reply, resolution, mention, merge or release."
